	{ q: 'Detection has not been measured, and one pilot was negative.', a: 'Precision, recall and delay against known faults are M2. A pilot using disagreement between parts to flag mislabelled samples was negative (AUROC ≈ 0.51 against ≈ 0.97 for plain per-sample loss), and V2 changed course because of it.' },
	{ q: 'The paper and the code disagree on one point.', a: 'The paper states a 30% cap on resets; the code does not enforce it. A correction is pending. The April 2026 suite that killed the predecessor has not yet been re-run on the current code.' },
	{ q: 'The external record is early.', a: 'Accepted at DeepMath 2026 (decision 30 September; presented 30 October 2026), and a reviewer for NeurIPS 2026 (3 October), for the Trustworthy AI for Good workshop in Paris on 12 December. The experiments are not yet independently replicated. Every reviewer request maps to a milestone.' },
];

const trail = [{ label: 'Home', href: '/' }, { label: 'Invest' }];

---

<Page title="Pre-seed: the round and the risks" description={"Pre-seed, $750K on a post-money SAFE at a $7.5M cap, 18 months, five milestones with pass lines written first. Neural networks that report what broke while they train, and fix it."} ogImagePath="/og/invest-v3.png" trail={trail}>
	<PageBanner
		eyebrow="INVEST"
		title="The system of record for what training did."
		trail={trail}
	/>

	<section class="section-tight container reveal">
		<div class="iv-brief">
			<p class="iv-brief-label">The whole thing, in one screen</p>
			<dl class="iv-brief-list">
				{brief.map((b) => (
					<div class="iv-brief-row">
						<dt>{b.k}</dt>
						<dd>{b.v}</dd>
					</div>
				))}
			</dl>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="section container">
		<div class="iv-thesis">
			<p class="iv-thesis-lead">
				Every model should arrive with a record of what its training did, part by part. Today none
				does.
			</p>
			<div class="iv-thesis-body">
				<p class="iv-thesis-p">
					When a training run breaks, the standard response is to rewind to a checkpoint, skip some
					data and try again. Trackers chart the loss; model-risk tools inspect the finished model.
					Nothing in between names the part that broke while it is breaking, so the cause is never
					written down and a validator inherits a black box.
				</p>
				<p class="iv-thesis-p">
					ORMAS watches every component while the model trains. When a part dies, its learning
					signal is exactly zero, and standard training cannot leave that trap. ORMAS names the part,
					resets only that part, and writes the change to a ledger: component, epoch, reason, size.
				</p>
				<p class="iv-thesis-turn">
					Don’t trust us: replay the run yourself at oxiedo.com/black-box. Every figure there is read
					from the archived run files; nothing is simulated in the browser.
				</p>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="band band--dark section reveal">
		<div class="container">
			<div class="iv-stats">
				{stats.map((s) => (
					<div class="iv-stat">
						<p class="iv-stat-figure tabular">
							{s.figure}{s.unit && <span class="iv-stat-unit">{s.unit}</span>}
						</p>
						<p class="iv-stat-label">{s.label}</p>
					</div>
				))}
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="section container reveal">
		<Eyebrow>WHY NOW</Eyebrow>
		<h2 class="iv-h2" id="iv-timeline-h">The demand event has a date on it.</h2>
		<p class="iv-lede">
			The usual answer to “why has nobody built this” is that the incentive did not exist. Here it
			is arriving on a legislated calendar, and an architecture cannot be retrofitted into a model
			that has already been trained, so it has to exist before the date, not after it.
		</p>

		<figure class="iv-chart" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-labelledby="iv-timeline-h">
			<svg
				viewBox={`0 0 ${CH.w} ${CH.h}`}
				class="iv-chart-svg"
				role="img"
				aria-label="Regulatory calendar from 2026 to 2031. SR 26-2 effective April 2026. EU AI Act Omnibus in force July 2026. EU AI Act Annex III high-risk obligations apply 2 December 2027. Annex I obligations apply 2 August 2028. European Health Data Space first phase 2029, full scope 2031."
			>
				{years.map((y) => (
					<g>
						<line
							x1={x(`${y}-01-01`)} y1={CH.top - 22}
							x2={x(`${y}-01-01`)} y2={CH.h - 20}
							class="iv-chart-grid"
						/>
						<text x={x(`${y}-01-01`)} y={CH.top - 30} class="iv-chart-year">{y}</text>
					</g>
				))}

				<line
					x1={x(today)} y1={CH.top - 22}
					x2={x(today)} y2={CH.h - 20}
					class="iv-chart-now"
				/>
				<text x={x(today)} y={CH.h - 6} class="iv-chart-nowlabel">TODAY</text>

				{events.map((e, i) => {
					const cy = CH.top + i * CH.rowH;
					return (
						<g>
							<text x={CH.labelW - 16} y={cy - 2} class="iv-chart-label">{e.label}</text>
							<text x={CH.labelW - 16} y={cy + 13} class="iv-chart-who">{e.who}</text>
							<line x1={CH.labelW} y1={cy + 1} x2={x(e.date) - 7} y2={cy + 1} class="iv-chart-lead" />
							<circle
								cx={x(e.date)} cy={cy + 1} r="5.5"
								class={e.past ? 'iv-chart-dot iv-chart-dot--past' : 'iv-chart-dot'}
							/>
						</g>
					);
				})}
			</svg>
			<figcaption class="iv-chart-cap">
				Dates in law as at October 2026. Filled marks have already taken effect.
			</figcaption>
		</figure>

		<p class="iv-note">
			Two of these have already happened. In the UK the PRA’s SS1/23 deliberately covers AI models,
			and in the US the FDA lets AI devices change only under a documented change plan. Banks are not
			ready: large EMEA banks run around 365 models, 67% use AI or machine learning, only 29% say
			their framework fits, and 75% put under 5% of staff on AI validation (Deloitte, 2025).
		</p>
	</section>

	<section class="section container reveal">
		<Eyebrow>THE MARKET</Eyebrow>
		<h2 class="iv-h2">A $19B market by 2035, and we know who signs.</h2>
		<p class="iv-lede">
			The reference market is AI model-risk management: $5.9B (2025) → $19.1B by 2035, growing
			12.5% a year, with 35% in finance. Model-risk spend is already a budget line. We sell into it
			from training.
		</p>
		<div class="iv-bench">
			{tamSamSom.map((t, i) => (
				<div class={i === tamSamSom.length - 1 ? 'iv-bench-row iv-bench-row--ours' : 'iv-bench-row'}>
					<p class="iv-bench-k">{t.k}</p>
					<p class="iv-bench-v tabular">{t.v}</p>
					<p class="iv-bench-note">{t.note}</p>
				</div>
			))}
		</div>
		<div class="iv-bench">
			{segments.map((seg) => (
				<div class="iv-bench-row">
					<p class="iv-bench-k">{seg.k}</p>
					<p class="iv-bench-v tabular">{seg.v}</p>
					<p class="iv-bench-note">{seg.note}</p>
				</div>
			))}
		</div>
		<p class="iv-note">
			Together that is $149M serviceable now, and the year-five target is 3.2% of it: $4.75M ARR.
			Adjacent markets are larger: AI governance software reaches $15.8B by 2030 (Forrester) and
			MLOps $16.6B by 2030, all inside $2.7T of AI spend in 2026.
		</p>
		<p class="iv-caveat">
			The counts are sourced. The prices and the year-five target are our hypotheses: no price has
			been put to a buyer yet, and M4 is where that changes.
		</p>
	</section>

	<section class="band band--surface section reveal">
		<div class="container">
			<Eyebrow>WHO SIGNS</Eyebrow>
			<h2 class="iv-h2">One wedge, one expansion.</h2>
			<p class="iv-lede">
				The wedge is the monitor and change record for an ML platform team. The expansion is the
				same record, read by a model-risk validator. An annual licence per team, run on the
				customer’s own machines: no seats, no usage meter, no hosted tier.
			</p>
			<div class="iv-moat">
				{roles.map((r) => (
					<article class="iv-moat-item">
						<h3 class="iv-moat-title">{r.title}</h3>
						<p class="iv-moat-body">{r.body}</p>
					</article>
				))}
			</div>
			<p class="iv-note">
				Records belong to the customer and export in a documented format, during the term and
				after it. Renewal is earned on new runs: monitoring, updates, support, and a version their
				validator has reviewed. The switching cost is re-validation, not lost history.
			</p>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="section container reveal">
		<Eyebrow>DEFENSIBILITY</Eyebrow>
		<h2 class="iv-h2">Why this is hard to copy, ranked honestly.</h2>
		<p class="iv-lede">
			Five advantages, each with what a competitor would need and where it stands today. The first
			two exist now. The third is what locks in, and it is earned in a first validation cycle, not
			claimed. A tracker could copy the second quickly; the first and third take runs and a
			validator’s review.
		</p>
		<div class="iv-moat">
			{moat.map((m) => (
				<article class="iv-moat-item">
					<h3 class="iv-moat-title">{m.k}</h3>
					<p class="iv-moat-body">{m.v}</p>
					<p class="iv-moat-body"><strong>Today:</strong> {m.status}</p>
				</article>
			))}
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="band band--surface section reveal">
		<div class="container">
			<Eyebrow>THE ALTERNATIVES</Eyebrow>
			<h2 class="iv-h2" id="iv-alternatives-h">Trackers chart training. Oxiedo records each fix.</h2>
			<p class="iv-lede">
				Our axis is a per-component record of each fix, made during training, on the customer’s
				machines. The tools a buyer already owns either watch the run or inspect the finished
				model; none of them names, resets and records the part that broke.
			</p>
			<div class="iv-table-wrap" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-labelledby="iv-alternatives-h">
				<table class="iv-table">
					<thead>
						<tr>
							<th scope="col">The buyer’s alternative</th>
							{altCols.map((c) => <th scope="col">{c}</th>)}
						</tr>
					</thead>
					<tbody>
						{alternatives.map((a) => (
							<tr class={a.ours ? 'iv-table-row--ours' : a.incumbent ? 'iv-table-row--lead' : undefined}>
								<th scope="row">{a.name}</th>
								{a.marks.map((m) => <td class="iv-table-mark">{m}</td>)}
							</tr>
						))}
					</tbody>
				</table>
			</div>
			<p class="iv-note">
				The category is being bought: Weights &amp; Biases by CoreWeave (about $1.7B, 2025), Arize
				by Dynatrace ($915M, 2026), Neptune by OpenAI (2025). And funded: Arize $70M, Fiddler $30M,
				Credo AI $21M, ValidMind $8.1M.
			</p>
			<p class="iv-note">
				The real rival is the substitute: rewind and retry is free and habitual, and the reset itself
				is open code. Our edge is a 383-experiment failure archive, data read inside the training
				loop, and a record that, once a validator accepts it, costs a re-validation to replace.
			</p>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="section container reveal">
		<Eyebrow>THE TEAM</Eyebrow>
		<h2 class="iv-h2" id="iv-skills-h">Ships fast, and tries to break the work first.</h2>
		<p class="iv-lede">
			Rokib Al Dhin Raadh built V1 alone. Dated and checkable: in April 2026 the founder’s own test suite
			killed the first design, and it was rebuilt; 383 controlled experiments across four model
			families; the replay demo shipped in September; the DeepMath 2026 poster accepted in September; a NeurIPS 2026 workshop reviewer in October; every baseline reviewers asked for run in October.
		</p>
		<div class="iv-table-wrap" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-labelledby="iv-skills-h">
			<table class="iv-table">
				<thead>
					<tr>
						<th scope="col">Skill the plan needs</th>
						<th scope="col">Today</th>
						<th scope="col">Evidence, or who covers it</th>
					</tr>
				</thead>
				<tbody>
					{skills.map((k) => (
						<tr>
							<th scope="row">{k.k}</th>
							<td class={k.state === 'Gap' ? 'iv-table-weak' : 'iv-table-note'}>{k.state}</td>
							<td>{k.who}</td>
						</tr>
					))}
				</tbody>
			</table>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="band band--surface section reveal">
		<div class="container">
			<Eyebrow>GO-TO-MARKET</Eyebrow>
			<h2 class="iv-h2" id="iv-funnel-h">20 buyer calls by month 4; 4 paid teams in year 2.</h2>
			<p class="iv-lede">
				Every stage has a number, an owner and a channel. Each is a hypothesis until contract three,
				when observed conversion rates replace it.
			</p>
			<div class="iv-table-wrap" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-labelledby="iv-funnel-h">
				<table class="iv-table">
					<thead>
						<tr>
							<th scope="col">Stage</th>
							<th scope="col">Year 1</th>
							<th scope="col">Year 2</th>
							<th scope="col">Year 3</th>
							<th scope="col">Owner</th>
						</tr>
					</thead>
					<tbody>
						{funnel.map((f) => (
							<tr>
								<th scope="row">{f.k}</th>
								<td class="tabular">{f.y1}</td>
								<td class="tabular">{f.y2}</td>
								<td class="tabular">{f.y3}</td>
								<td class="iv-table-note">{f.owner}</td>
							</tr>
						))}
					</tbody>
				</table>
			</div>
			<p class="iv-note">
				Of the $750K, $223.5K is go-to-market. Year one is expected to buy 60 conversations and three
				design partners at $0 revenue: about $2K per conversation and $40K per design partner.
			</p>
			<div class="iv-moat">
				{payment.map((p) => (
					<article class="iv-moat-item">
						<h3 class="iv-moat-title">{p.k}</h3>
						<p class="iv-moat-body">{p.v}</p>
					</article>
				))}
			</div>
			<p class="iv-caveat">
				All stage numbers, prices and pilot terms are hypotheses, set before any contract.
			</p>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="section container reveal">
		<Eyebrow>THE NUMBER</Eyebrow>
		<h2 class="iv-h2">$750K buys five tested milestones in 18 months.</h2>
		<p class="iv-lede">
			Priced against the market rather than picked, and priced below it on purpose. The Carta
			benchmarks are below, and every line of the round is costed underneath them.
		</p>
		<div class="iv-bench">
			{benchmarks.map((b, i) => (
				<div class={i === benchmarks.length - 1 ? 'iv-bench-row iv-bench-row--ours' : 'iv-bench-row'}>
					<p class="iv-bench-k">{b.k}</p>
					<p class="iv-bench-v tabular">{b.v}</p>
					<p class="iv-bench-note">{b.note}</p>
				</div>
			))}
		</div>
		<p class="iv-note">
			The round is sized to the next results, not to the whole plan. Research runs only where the
			product needs an answer, and the Dhaka cost base is what lets $750K carry three hires for 18
			months. If an accelerator or programme (Entrepreneur First, Antler and similar) leads, its
			terms replace the instrument; the milestones stay the same.
		</p>
	</section>

	<section class="section container reveal">
		<Eyebrow>THE MILESTONES</Eyebrow>
		<h2 class="iv-h2" id="iv-milestones-h">Five milestones, each with a pass line written first.</h2>
		<p class="iv-lede">
			A failed milestone gets reported. Months are counted from close, assumed December 2026; M5 is
			pinned to the NeurIPS 2027 deadline in mid-May.
		</p>
		<div class="iv-table-wrap" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-labelledby="iv-milestones-h">
			<table class="iv-table">
				<thead>
					<tr>
						<th scope="col"></th>
						<th scope="col">Milestone</th>
						<th scope="col">Passes if</th>
						<th scope="col">Month</th>
					</tr>
				</thead>
				<tbody>
					{milestones.map((m) => (
						<tr>
							<th scope="row">{m.id}</th>
							<td>{m.k}</td>
							<td class="iv-table-note">{m.pass}</td>
							<td class="tabular">{m.month}</td>
						</tr>
					))}
				</tbody>
			</table>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="section container reveal">
		<Eyebrow>USE OF FUNDS</Eyebrow>
		<h2 class="iv-h2">The $750K, line by line.</h2>
		<p class="iv-lede">
			Every line names the milestone it pays for. Runway is {raise.runway}, on a Dhaka cost base,
			with the Delaware C-corp formed at close.
		</p>
		<ol class="iv-uses">
			{uses.map((u) => (
				<li class="iv-use">
					<div class="iv-use-head">
						<span class="iv-use-n tabular">{u.n}</span>
						<div class="iv-use-heading">
							<h3 class="iv-use-title">{u.title}</h3>
							<p class="iv-use-alloc">{u.unit}</p>
						</div>
						<span class="iv-use-amount tabular">{u.amount}</span>
						<span class="iv-use-removes">{u.removes}</span>
					</div>
					{u.pct > 0 && (
						<div class="iv-use-bar" aria-hidden="true">
							<span class="iv-use-bar-fill" style={`width:${u.pct}%`}></span>
						</div>
					)}
					<p class="iv-use-body">{u.body}</p>
					<p class="iv-use-milestone">
						<span class="iv-use-milestone-k">Pays for</span>
						{u.milestone}
					</p>
				</li>
			))}
		</ol>
	</section>

	<section class="band band--surface section reveal">
		<div class="container">
			<Eyebrow>THREE YEARS</Eyebrow>
			<h2 class="iv-h2" id="iv-projection-h">Three years, with year one at $0 revenue.</h2>
			<p class="iv-lede">
				Year one is months 1–12 after close. Every figure is a planning assumption, not a forecast
				from data.
			</p>
			<div class="iv-table-wrap" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-labelledby="iv-projection-h">
				<table class="iv-table">
					<thead>
						<tr>
							<th scope="col"></th>
							<th scope="col">Year 1</th>
							<th scope="col">Year 2</th>
							<th scope="col">Year 3</th>
							<th scope="col">Assumption</th>
						</tr>
					</thead>
					<tbody>
						{plan.map((r) => (
							<tr class={r.lead ? 'iv-table-row--lead' : undefined}>
								<th scope="row">{r.k}</th>
								<td class="tabular">{r.y1}</td>
								<td class="tabular">{r.y2}</td>
								<td class="tabular">{r.y3}</td>
								<td class="iv-table-note">{r.note}</td>
							</tr>
						))}
					</tbody>
				</table>
			</div>
			<p class="iv-note">
				Gross margin is high because nothing is hosted: cost of revenue is deployment engineering
				and support. Unit economics below are hypotheses until the first three paid contracts
				replace them; after contracts one to three, CAC and payback are recomputed from actual cost,
				and any channel above $120K CAC is dropped.
			</p>
			<div class="iv-table-wrap" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Unit economics, hypotheses">
				<table class="iv-table">
					<thead>
						<tr>
							<th scope="col">Unit economics (hypothesis)</th>
							<th scope="col">Monitor</th>
							<th scope="col">Model-risk record</th>
							<th scope="col">Blended, year 3</th>
						</tr>
					</thead>
					<tbody>
						{unitEcon.map((u) => (
							<tr class={u.lead ? 'iv-table-row--lead' : undefined}>
								<th scope="row">{u.k}</th>
								<td class="tabular">{u.m}</td>
								<td class="tabular">{u.r}</td>
								<td class="tabular">{u.b}</td>
							</tr>
						))}
					</tbody>
				</table>
			</div>
			<p class="iv-note">
				Blended CAC is $840K of sales and marketing over three years divided by 12 paid customers.
				The monitor at the blended $70K CAC is 3.4×, against a 3× benchmark for healthy.
			</p>
			<p class="iv-caveat">
				The seed is raised from month 12 on M1–M5 results; the model assumes month 15. The buffer
				covers three more months if it slips.
			</p>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="section container reveal">
		<Eyebrow>CAPITAL DISCIPLINE</Eyebrow>
		<h2 class="iv-h2">What this round is deliberately not spent on.</h2>
		<p class="iv-lede">
			A use-of-funds is only as credible as the things it refuses.
		</p>
		<div class="iv-not">
			{notSpending.map((n) => (
				<article class="iv-not-item">
					<h3 class="iv-not-k">{n.k}</h3>
					<p class="iv-not-v">{n.v}</p>
				</article>
			))}
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="section container reveal">
		<Eyebrow>THE LADDER</Eyebrow>
		<h2 class="iv-h2">What is already removed, and what this round removes next.</h2>
		<ul class="iv-ladder">
			{derisked.map((d) => (
				<li class={d.done ? 'iv-rung iv-rung--done' : 'iv-rung'}>
					<span class="iv-rung-state">{d.done ? 'REMOVED' : 'LIVE'}</span>
					<div>
						<h3 class="iv-rung-k">{d.k}</h3>
						<p class="iv-rung-v">{d.v}</p>
					</div>
				</li>
			))}
		</ul>
	</section>

	<section class="band band--surface section reveal">
		<div class="container">
			<Eyebrow>THE RISK REGISTER</Eyebrow>
			<h2 class="iv-h2">What is not established, and where ORMAS loses.</h2>
			<p class="iv-lede">
				None of this is disclosed reluctantly. An investor who finds these in week three discounts
				everything else on the page; an investor who reads them here is evaluating the same
				company with better information.
			</p>
